@1100 = ~ARCHER: The Archer is the epitome of skill with ranged weapons: an expert marksman able to make difficult shots while sacrificing durability, armor and melee versatility.

Advantages:
- +1 bonus to hit and damage rolls with missile weapons at level 1 and every 4 levels thereafter.
- +1 bonus to Armor Class vs. missile weapons every 6 levels.
- +5% chance to score a critical hit at levels 13 and 18.
- May achieve Grand Mastery (5 slots) in longbows, shortbows and crossbows.
- Farsighted: +2 visual range.
- May toggle Rapid Shot while a bow or crossbow is equipped: gains +1 attack per round while suffering a -4 penalty to hit with ranged attacks. From level 12 onward the penalty is reduced to -2.
- Gains a shared Special Shot pool at level 4, with +1 use every 4 levels thereafter. At level 4 the Archer may choose Called Shot or Rooting Shot; at level 8 Power Shot and Explosive Shot are added to the same pool.
- May use Conjure Elemental Ammunition once per day every 8 levels, starting at level 4.

Disadvantages:
- Hit Die: d8.
- May not wear metal armor.
- Suffers a -3 THAC0 penalty when using melee weapons.
- May only become Proficient (one slot) with melee weapons.
- May not gain proficiency in Two-Weapon Style.
- May not use Charm Animal.

Archer Revised v0.1-dev establishes the standalone EET core. Manyshot, Sniper and the revised high-level abilities are being implemented as native Archer Revised resources rather than copied from another mod.~

@3000 = ~Rapid Shot~
@3001 = ~Rapid Shot
Choose whether to activate or deactivate Rapid Shot. While active, the stance grants +1 attack per round only while a bow or crossbow is equipped, but imposes a -4 penalty to ranged THAC0. From level 12 onward the penalty is reduced to -2.~
@3002 = ~Activate Rapid Shot~
@3003 = ~Activate Rapid Shot
Enters the Rapid Shot stance. The stance remains active until manually deactivated.~
@3004 = ~Deactivate Rapid Shot~
@3005 = ~Deactivate Rapid Shot
Ends the Rapid Shot stance and removes its attack-rate and ranged accuracy modifiers.~

@3100 = ~Special Shot~
@3101 = ~Special Shot
Select one shot technique. At this level the available techniques are Called Shot and Rooting Shot. All Special Shot techniques consume the same pool of daily uses.~
@3102 = ~Special Shot
Select one shot technique. Available techniques are Called Shot, Rooting Shot, Power Shot and Explosive Shot. All Special Shot techniques consume the same pool of daily uses.~

@3200 = ~Called Shot~
@3201 = ~Called Shot
For the next 10 seconds, every successful ranged attack applies the following non-cumulative effects to the target for 1 turn, according to the Archer's level:
4th level: Dexterity is reduced to 50%.
8th level: Movement rate is also reduced to 25%.
12th level: The target also loses 1 attack per round.
16th level: Every successful hit also deals +2 missile damage.
Repeated hits refresh these effects rather than stacking them.~
